        {
          "source_id": "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:document:660d269ce0e0ee226093dd3c78c292d98b7ef7de1af61f8431adecf82778afc6",
          "quote": "Material discrepancies between the name recorded on the application, the applicant's evidence of U.S. citizenship/non-citizen U.S. nationality, or the evidence of identity must be documented by submission of one or more of the documents listed in this section (see an exception for married names in 8 FAM 403.1-4(C)). Acceptable means of documenting a material name change include (per 22 CFR 51.25):",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 400
        },
        {
          "source_id": "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:document:660d269ce0e0ee226093dd3c78c292d98b7ef7de1af61f8431adecf82778afc6",
          "quote": "(5) Documentation of customary usage.",
          "start": 625,
          "end": 662
        }
      ],
      "rationale": "The claim attempts to combine the core documentation requirement with several acceptable document types into a single claim. However, its explicit fields omit item (5) Documentation of customary usage from both the alternative list and summary, and completely fail to extract the exception for married names under 8 FAM 403.1-4(C). Furthermore, actor, action, and object are left blank, and the specific scope defining the three-way discrepancy is missing from the explicit scope fields.",
      "claim_sha256": "b1f1a6d48d80beb9485f1124457bc253a6ff53ecbd70c8086445fd319ba7d90f",
      "dimensions": {
        "summary": "error",
        "actor": "error",
        "support": "correct",
        "scope": "error",
        "links": "correct",
        "boundary": "error",
        "modality": "correct",
        "action": "error",
        "object": "error",
        "alternatives": "error",
        "thresholds": "not_applicable"
      }
    }
  ],
